    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm looking at a 2022 F-150 in the shop. Customer is complaining about the transmission slipping under load. I've got the scan tool hooked up and I'm seeing some really weird irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit during the shifts. What are the most likely things causing these kinds of pressure fluctuations in a modern automatic like this?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those irregular pressure spikes suggest issues within the transmission's hydraulic system. Common culprits include a failing solenoid pack, which can cause inconsistent control over fluid flow, or low/contaminated transmission fluid. Furthermore, worn valve body components can prevent smooth, regulated pressure buildup during load changes.",
