    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i checked the fluid and it actually looks pretty clean, no burnt smell either. if it's not the fluid itself, could it be a sensor issue? like the line pressure sensor or something reading the wrong thing and causing the TCM to hunt for the right pressure? or is it more likely a mechanical blockage in the valve body?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A faulty line pressure sensor or other input sensors is a very strong possibility, as inaccurate readings can cause the Transmission Control Module (TCM) to overcorrect, leading to pressure hunting. However, internal mechanical blockage within the valve body remains a highly probable cause, even with clean fluid. To narrow it down, check the wiring integrity and connector pins for any signs of corrosion or damage.",
