    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "wiring looks fine and pins are clean. i'm starting to think it might be something erratic that only happens under specific load/temp combos. it's driving me crazy because it's so random. is there anything else that could cause these sudden, unexplainable spikes that don't seem to follow a clear pattern?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the issue is truly erratic and load-dependent, you should investigate the clutch pack pressure regulators within the valve body. Sometimes, a sticking or hardening clutch pack can momentarily demand excessive pressure, causing spikes until it properly engages or slips. Also, check the internal modulator or torque converter lock-up clutch for minor sticking issues, as these can manifest as transient pressure anomalies.",
      "source": "target",
